DTSTART:20260910T152742Z
DTEND:20260910T153742Z
SUMMARY:(1832) Mrkos hides a mag 12.5 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(1832) Mrkos hides a magnitude 12.5 star\, seen from Durg.\nThe
  predicted edge passes 5 km to the W\, so a miss is likely — but a chord
  from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClosest appr
 oach 21:02:42 IST\, give or take 10 s. The star is 44° up in the SSW · d
 ark sky.\nIt fades 4.1 magnitudes for up to 6.6 s on the centre line\, and
  the path is 29 km wide\, give or take 28 km.\nFinder chart\, the map and 
 the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026-09#2026-09-10-183
 2-mrkos-239232
